course: dictionary
lesson: 15101
title: Ruminate: thinking deeply, and going round in circles
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To ruminate means to think about something for a long time. Thinking deeply can be a good thing, like when a writer ruminates on a story before she finishes it. «Mia sat by the window and ruminated on what her teacher had said.» Mia is thinking hard and slowly, not rushing.
explain: Sometimes ruminating is not helpful. «Ben kept ruminating about the mistake he made, going over it again and again.» Here the thinking goes round in circles and the worry does not get smaller. When you notice this, try talking to someone you trust, such as a parent, a friend or a teacher.
explain: Ruminate also has a science meaning. «The cow lay in the field and ruminated, slowly chewing its food again.» Cows, sheep and goats bring food back up from their stomach and chew it again. This is called chewing the cud, and animals that do it are called ruminants.
explain: To check the meaning, swap a simple idea into the sentence. In «Mia ruminated on her teacher's words», try «Mia thought deeply about her teacher's words». If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Look at the clues: is the thinking calm and deep, or is it stuck and worried?
fact: Ruminate is a verb, so its forms are ruminates, ruminated and ruminating.
fact: «Ruminate on» and «ruminate about» are common phrases, as in «ruminate on an idea».
fact: To ruminate can mean thinking deeply for a long time, in a calm or helpful way.
fact: To ruminate can also mean going over the same worries again and again, which is usually negative.
fact: Ruminants, such as cows, sheep and goats, have a stomach with four parts and chew the cud.
exercise: «The cow lay under a tree and ruminated, slowly chewing its food again.» What does ruminated mean here? | *To chew food again after swallowing it | To run fast across the field | To shout loudly at the farmer | To sleep under a tree
exercise: «Ben kept ruminating about the mistake, going over it again and again.» What does ruminating mean here? | Forgetting it at once | *Going over the same worry again and again | Playing football happily | Cooking a big dinner
exercise: Which of these animals is a ruminant, one that chews the cud? | Lion | *Goat | Shark | Eagle
test: «Mia sat by the window and ruminated on what her teacher had said.» Which phrase is closest in meaning to ruminated on? | Forgot all about | Laughed loudly at | *Thought deeply about | Ran away from
test: Which kind of thinking does ruminate describe when it is negative? | Writing a long story | Thinking about a fun holiday | Singing a happy song | *Going round in circles over a worry
exam: «Ella ruminated about the test all night, until she talked to her mum and felt calmer.» According to the sentence, what helped Ella? | Shouting at the test paper | *Talking to her mum | Ignoring the problem for ever | Eating a big breakfast
